# Foilio — Privacy Policy

**Last updated: 3 September 2026**
**Applies to: Foilio for Android (`com.leoseverini.foilio`)**

Foilio is a catalogue for a Magic: The Gathering collection. It runs on your
phone, stores your collection on your phone, and works with the network turned
off.

This policy says what leaves the device, what does not, and who else is
involved. It is written to be read, not to be survived.

---

## The short version

- **Foilio has no account and no server.** There is nothing to sign up for, and
  no copy of your collection anywhere but your own device and any backup you
  export yourself.
- **Your collection never leaves the device** unless you export a backup and
  choose where to send it.
- **Photos from the camera are never uploaded.** Card recognition happens
  entirely on the phone, against a card database that ships inside the app.
  Frames are held in memory for a fraction of a second and then discarded.
- **The free version shows ads,** which are served by Google AdMob. AdMob
  collects data — this is the one part of the app that does. What it collects
  is set out below.
- **Foilio Pro removes the ads,** and with them every ad-related data flow. It
  is a one-time purchase handled by Google Play.

---

## What Foilio stores on your device

All of it stays on the device, in the app's own private storage.

| What | Where | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Your containers, cards, quantities, conditions, tags, notes, decks, pull records, audits and wishlist | `user.sqlite` | This is your collection. It is the app. |
| The card database — names, sets, prices, art hashes, image URLs | `cards.sqlite` | So search and the scanner work offline. Shipped with the app; identical for every user. |
| Your settings, the day's scan count, and whether you own Foilio Pro | Android's preference store | Small values. The scan count resets every day and is not included in a backup. |

Nothing in this list is transmitted anywhere by Foilio. Uninstalling the app
deletes all of it — Android removes an app's private storage with the app, so
**export a backup first if you want to keep your collection.**

## What Foilio does not collect

To be explicit, because "we take your privacy seriously" is not information:

- No account, email address, name or phone number. You are never asked.
- No analytics, telemetry, crash reporting or usage statistics. There is no
  code in the app that reports how you use it, because there is nowhere for it
  to report to.
- No contacts, location, calendar, files, microphone or call data.
- No advertising profile built by us. We never see AdMob's data; Google serves
  the ads and reports us a number.

## Permissions, and what each is for

| Permission | What it is for |
|---|---|
| `CAMERA` | Recognising a card you hold up. Frames are processed on the device and discarded; nothing is written to storage or uploaded. Declining it leaves every other part of the app working. |
| `INTERNET` | Three things: loading card images from Scryfall while you browse, checking whether a newer card database has been published, and requesting ads. With no network the app still opens, searches, scans and files cards. |
| `VIBRATE` | The confirmation tap when a card is recognised. |
| `AD_ID` (`com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID`) | Lets AdMob read the device's advertising ID. Present because the app serves ads. |

There is no storage permission: backups are handed to Android's own share sheet
and imports come through Android's file picker, so Foilio only ever sees the
one file you pick.

## When Foilio contacts the network, and who it reaches

Four occasions, and no others.

**1. Card images, from Scryfall.** When you browse cards, thumbnails are loaded
from `scryfall.com`. Scryfall receives the request — which means your IP address
and which card image you asked for — and their privacy policy applies to it.
Foilio stores image *URLs*, never image files. Scryfall's policy:
<https://scryfall.com/docs/privacy-policy>

**2. The card database update check, from GitHub.** Foilio asks a small file on
`raw.githubusercontent.com` whether a newer card database exists. The request
carries your IP address and nothing about you or your collection. GitHub's
privacy statement applies. **A download never starts on its own** — a new card
database is around 34 MB and always needs a tap.

**3. Ads, from Google AdMob.** Free version only. Covered in its own section
below.

**4. The purchase, through Google Play.** Only when you tap to buy Foilio Pro or
to restore a purchase. Google Play handles the entire transaction; Foilio is
told only whether you own the product. **No payment details ever reach this app**
— it cannot see your card number, and does not ask for one.

Notably absent: card recognition. The scanner never calls Scryfall or anything
else. It matches against the database already on the phone.

## Ads (free version only)

The free version of Foilio shows a banner at the top of the screen and, when
you choose to watch one for ten extra scans, a full-screen ad. Both are served
by **Google AdMob**. The full-screen ad only ever appears after you tap a
button asking for it.

To serve an ad, Google may collect and process:

- the device's **advertising ID** (a resettable identifier — Android
  Settings › Privacy › Ads lets you reset or delete it);
- **device and app information** — model, operating system version, app
  version, language, coarse region;
- your **IP address**, from which Google infers approximate location;
- **ad interactions** — which ads were shown, viewed or tapped.

Google uses this to select ads, to measure them, and to prevent fraud.
Depending on your consent and your region, it may be used for personalised
advertising. We do not receive any of it, and we do not send Google anything
about your collection — Foilio does not have a user identifier to send.

- Google's advertising policy: <https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads>
- How Google uses data from partner sites and apps:
  <https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites>

**Consent.** In the EEA, the UK and Switzerland, Foilio shows Google's own
consent form before requesting its first ad, and your answer is stored on the
device. You can change it at any time: **Settings › Ad privacy options**. Where
that row is not shown, it is because the consent framework reports that no
consent is required in your region.

**Turning ads off entirely.** Buy Foilio Pro. With Pro, no ad is ever
requested, the ad SDK makes no ad calls, and the banner is removed from the
layout rather than left blank.

## Foilio Pro, and purchases

Foilio Pro is a **one-time purchase** (product id `foilio_pro_unlock`), not a
subscription. It removes the free plan's limits and all ads.

The purchase is processed by Google Play Billing. Google receives and handles
everything about the payment; Foilio receives a yes or no and remembers it on
the device. Google Play's terms and privacy policy govern the transaction, the
receipt and any refund: <https://policies.google.com/privacy>

Because the entitlement is remembered on the device and there is no account,
**"Restore purchase" on the Foilio Pro screen** is how a reinstall or a new
phone gets the unlock back. It asks Google Play what your Play account already
owns. It never charges again.

## Backups and exports, which are yours to place

Foilio can export your whole collection as a single file, and can import one
back. Both are entirely under your control:

- an **export** is handed to Android's share sheet. Where it goes — Google
  Drive, email, a messaging app, local storage — is your choice, and Foilio has
  no visibility into it and does not keep a copy;
- an **import** comes through Android's file picker, so the app can read only
  the one file you select.

A backup file contains your collection in plain, readable JSON. It is not
encrypted. Treat it like any other document: if you would not post it publicly,
do not put it somewhere public.

Backups do not include the card database (it ships with the app), your
settings, or the day's scan count.

## Children

Foilio is not directed at children and is rated for a general audience. It does
not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, of any age. In the Play
Console it is declared as not primarily child-directed; ad content is requested
with Google's standard content settings.

## Your rights over data

Because Foilio holds no data about you on any server, the usual requests have
unusually direct answers:

- **Access or export** — the backup export produces everything the app holds.
- **Deletion** — uninstalling the app deletes it all. Within the app, any
  container, deck, card or wish can be deleted individually.
- **Advertising data** — held by Google, not by us. Reset or delete the
  advertising ID in Android Settings › Privacy › Ads, change your consent in
  Foilio's Settings › Ad privacy options, or use Google's own controls at
  <https://myadcenter.google.com>.
- **Purchase records** — held by Google Play; managed from your Play account.

There is no request to send us, because there is nothing on our side to act on.

## Card data, and whose it is

Card names, text, images and prices come from **Scryfall**
(<https://scryfall.com>), used with attribution as their terms require. Prices
are a dated estimate from a Scryfall bulk dump, not a valuation.

